          "kicker": "Eligibility check",
          "heading": "Jeremy Ward's France eligibility still awaits World Rugby special permission",
          "body": "Jeremy Ward remains in limbo over whether he can play for France at all. The 30-year-old is in the 42-man squad but will train without featuring against Fiji, the Springboks or Argentina, and his eligibility depends on World Rugby granting special permission. He will only complete his five-year residency in 2027, and his four Junior Springboks appearances at the 2016 U20 Championship tie him to South Africa, which was then designated their second national team. No World Rugby decision has been reported."
        },
