          "kicker": "Squad call-up",
          "heading": "Ollie Leatherbarrow earns first Scotland call-up in 37-man Nations Championship squad",
          "body": "Newcastle back-rower Ollie Leatherbarrow has been called up by Scotland for the first time, and the English-born 24-year-old is the only uncapped player in Gregor Townsend's 37-man squad for the Nations Championship. He qualifies through his grandmother from Perth and has 11 Scotland U20 caps, according to Planet Rugby. Townsend's group also brings back Huw Jones, who missed the July tour through injury, while Grant Gilchrist, recently back from injury, is a notable absentee."
