        {
          "kicker": "Squad origins",
          "heading": "BBC analysis: 76 of Wales' past 100 debutants born in Wales",
          "body": "The BBC has traced the past 100 men to make their Wales debuts, and the pathway is less Welsh than the badge suggests. Of the 100, 76 were born in Wales, 17 in England and seven elsewhere, but 78 learned their rugby up to age 16 in Wales, with Cardiff's catchment supplying 30. Dewi Lake, Adam Beard and Jac Morgan now play outside Wales, while Louis Rees-Zammit and Dafydd Jenkins made the journey across the border."
        },
