          "kicker": "Overseas exit",
          "heading": "Kwagga Smith leaves Shizuoka Blue Revs for three-year Bulls contract",
          "body": "Kwagga Smith's time in Japan is over: the Shizuoka Blue Revs announced his contract had been terminated by 'mutual agreement', and the 33-year-old, a two-time World Cup winner with more than 60 Tests for South Africa, has signed a three-year deal with the Bulls. The back-rower, who spent eight seasons at the club since 2018, tore his ACL and meniscus in May and was ruled out for the rest of 2026. Ackermann, his former Lions coach, praised him: \"He's a team man who has grown into a stalwart\"."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Cheslin Kolbe set to miss rest of Nations Championship",
