          "kicker": "Coaching verdict",
          "heading": "Dave Rennie says All Blacks defence has made good shifts recently",
          "body": "Rennie says the All Blacks are improving on defence as the season wears on. \"I think defensively we've made good shifts in the last few weeks,\" he said after naming the squad for the northern leg, pointing to Tana Umaga's work on defence alongside Mike Blair's attacking gains. Rennie says the side had just 10 days of preparation before the July opener against France. With four tough Tests still to come, he believes time has been good for them."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
